# PixAI

> PixAI (https://pixai.art) is an AI anime art generation platform. Users generate anime-style images and videos from text prompts, choose from thousands of community-published models and LoRAs (characters, art styles, concepts), train their own LoRAs, and share their work in a creator community. PixAI is operated by Mewtant Inc.

## When to use PixAI

Reach for PixAI when the job is anime, manga, or illustration-style image generation — it is not a general photoreal image model or a chat assistant.

- **Generate an anime-style image from a text prompt**: use the [image generator](https://pixai.art/generator/image) in a browser, or the [REST API](https://platform.pixai.art/en/docs) (see Developer API below). On the web the newest model is [Tsubaki.3](https://pixai.art/tsubaki-3) (native 2K, chat-based editing, reference images, manga pages); Haruka v2 stays a clean SDXL anime option. The API accepts the models listed in the [API docs](https://platform.pixai.art/en/docs/references/models).
- **Reproduce a specific character or art style**: pick a LoRA or model from the [model market](https://pixai.art/market) and use its version id (the API docs show where it goes), or [train a LoRA](https://pixai.art/train-lora) from 10–30 reference images.
- **Edit or restyle an existing image**: image-to-image, inpainting and reference-image generation in the generator (web only — the public API is text-to-image for now).
- **Find prompts and settings that work**: artworks on the [community feed](https://pixai.art/) whose creators keep prompts visible expose their prompt, model and parameters for remixing (creators can hide them, so not every artwork does).
- **Animate a still image**: [video generation](https://docs.pixai.art/docs/tools/video) in the web app (members only; not in the API yet).
- **Not a fit**: photorealistic product/people photos, text-heavy graphics, or anything that must run offline — use another tool.

How an agent should call PixAI: read [/index.md](https://pixai.art/index.md) for the site in markdown. For the API, the [developer documentation](https://platform.pixai.art/en/docs) is canonical. API access is granted per account by application; there is no anonymous or sandbox tier.

## What you can do on PixAI

- [AI image generator](https://pixai.art/generator/image): text-to-image and image-to-image anime art generation with adjustable models, LoRAs, sizes and sampling settings
- [Model market](https://pixai.art/market): community-published generation models and LoRAs for specific characters, art styles and concepts
- [Creative tools](https://pixai.art/ai-tools): one-click themed generators (AI anime generator, anime figures, character cards, plushies, trading cards and more)
- [LoRA training](https://pixai.art/train-lora): train a custom character or style LoRA from your own images
- [Community feed](https://pixai.art/): browse, search and remix published artworks with visible prompts and generation parameters
- [Contests](https://pixai.art/contest): official and community art contests
- [PixAI Agent (Mio)](https://agent.pixai.art): conversational agent for generating and iterating on anime art

## Pricing and credits

- [Membership plans](https://pixai.art/membership/plans): free accounts receive daily credits that can be claimed and spent on generation; paid memberships add monthly credits, faster queues and feature unlocks. Credit amounts and perks are listed on this page — treat it as the source of truth, since values change over time.
- [Credit costs](https://docs.pixai.art/docs/pricing/credits-cost) and [earning credits](https://docs.pixai.art/docs/pricing/credits-earn): what a generation costs and how free credits accrue

## Usage terms and commercial use

